error[ffi_parameter_type]: `p` of `take_a` is declared a different kind of thing from the header's `struct a *` — clang read the header, and the two do not convert
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-570-a-handle-of-another-tag-is-refused-through-the-pragma.hero:18:5
     |
  18 |     function take_a(p: B) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: §4.19: a parameter is declared as what the header says. `struct a *` has no name in this language — if it is a struct, declare it as a `record` inside this same `extern` group and the header owns its layout
